  <wpt lat="34.853" lon="136.4">
    <name>Seki Station</name>
    <desc>rail-bailout · Last practical rail before Suzuka Pass in the westbound direction. Service frequency unverified and probably sparse. · demonstration / unverified</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.964" lon="136.166">
    <name>Kibukawa Station (Shiga side)</name>
    <desc>rail-bailout · First rail on the descent side of Suzuka. Position approximate. · demonstration / unverified</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.017" lon="135.96">
    <name>Kusatsu Station</name>
    <desc>rail-bailout · demonstration / unverified</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.006" lon="135.865">
    <name>Otsu Station</name>
    <desc>rail-bailout · demonstration / unverified</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.183" lon="139.009">
    <name>Hakone Pass IC — highway shoulder</name>
    <desc>hazard · Route 1, Hakone Shindo, old-road approaches and the Ashinoko Skyline access converge. Several hundred metres without sidewalk plus an unprotected crossing near the Shindo merge. The green pedestrian paint is paint: no curb, no barrier, no separation. Kevin and Kai ran this section in 2018. · demonstration / unverified</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.223" lon="139.04">
    <name>Hiryu Falls — Ashinoyu nature trail</name>
    <desc>hazard · Steep 2.3 km maintained nature trail. Kanagawa Prefecture advises against use during or just after rain; parts are prone to crumbling. · demonstration / unverified</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.693" lon="137.585">
    <name>Hamanako bridge crossings</name>
    <desc>hazard · Exposed to wind. Pedestrian legality and shoulder quality unverified bridge by bridge. · demonstration / unverified</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.830815" lon="138.143903">
    <name>Oi River crossing</name>
    <desc>river-crossing · medium / imported</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.095" lon="136.8">
    <name>Miya to Kuwana — Seven-ri gap</name>
    <desc>ferry-gap · Any land substitute needs pedestrian legality and shoulder quality checked bridge by bridge before it is walked. · demonstration / unverified</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.893957" lon="136.336802">
    <name>Suzuka Pass</name>
    <desc>hazard · Roughly 378 m saddle. Exposed, cool, windy; the Mie-side approach feels remote. Low rail redundancy on both sides. · medium / imported</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.213298" lon="139.063847">
    <name>Hatajuku — water and food</name>
    <desc>water · DEMONSTRATION PLACEMARK. Availability and hours entirely unverified. Do not plan the Hakone day around this. · medium / imported</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.852433" lon="136.392485">
    <name>Seki-juku — last resupply before Suzuka</name>
    <desc>water · DEMONSTRATION PLACEMARK. Availability and hours entirely unverified. · medium / imported</desc>
  </wpt>
